<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Multimedia Magic</title>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>🎬 Multimedia Magic</h1>
  <p>This webpage shows how audio and video can bring a page to life in a fun and engaging way.</p>

  <h2>Listen to the Sound</h2>
  <p>Use the player below to enjoy the audio clip.</p>

  <audio controls loop>
    <source src="music.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
    Your browser does not support the audio element.
  </audio>

  <h2>Watch the Visual Story</h2>
  <p>The video below adds movement and makes the content more exciting to explore.</p>

  <video width="500" height="300" controls loop poster="poster.png">
    <source src="video.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    Your browser does not support the video element.
  </video>

  <h2>Why Use Audio and Video?</h2>
  <p>The <strong>audio</strong> tag is used for sound files, while the <strong>video</strong> tag is used for moving visuals on a webpage.</p>

</body>
</html>
